{
  "name": "Knowledge Assistant — Drive/Notion ingest → pgvector",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 📚 Knowledge ingest → pgvector (production path)\n\n**What it does** — every 6 hours (or on demand) pulls docs that changed since the last run from **Google Drive** (a KB folder of Google Docs) and **Notion** (a KB database), normalises them, splits them into heading-aware chunks (~900 chars, 150 overlap), embeds each chunk with **OpenAI text-embedding-3-small** (1536-d) and **upserts** them into **Supabase / pgvector** (`kb_chunks`). Stale chunks of edited docs are pruned, then the watermark is saved.\n\n**Idempotent** — `chunk_id = docId#index` + `content_hash`; unchanged chunks are skipped, re-runs are safe.\n\n**Env vars (no secrets in this file)**\n`KB_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID` · `NOTION_TOKEN` · `NOTION_KB_DATABASE_ID` · `OPENAI_API_KEY` · `SUPABASE_URL` · `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`\nCredential: *Google Drive OAuth2* on the two Drive HTTP nodes.\nCode nodes need `NODE_FUNCTION_ALLOW_BUILTIN=crypto`.\n\n**Schema** — run `supabase/schema.sql` first (tables, HNSW index, `match_kb_chunks` hybrid search, `prune_doc_chunks`).\n\nUsing only one source? Delete the other branch (Merge then passes a single input through).\n\nThe watermark lives in workflow static data, which only persists for **active** (production) executions; manual runs re-ingest everything (safe, just slower).",
        "height": 620,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "28e1225e-bf86-4d40-ab58-6b91fe99ac0b",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -420,
